From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] linux: link plugin libraries with RUNPATH $ORIGIN, not the build tree

Class:   UPSTREAMABLE FIX (to Flutter's Linux app template; the same change as
         ours/localsend 0004 and open-chess 0004).
Applies: musicpod v2.16.0 (patch -p1 from the repository root).
Fixes:   plugin libraries reach the bundle through install(FILES) and keep
         CMake's build RUNPATH, the absolute flutter/ephemeral directory of
         the build tree. Linked with RUNPATH $ORIGIN instead.
---
--- a/linux/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/linux/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -74,6 +74,16 @@
 # them to the application.
 include(flutter/generated_plugins.cmake)
 
+# Plugin libraries reach the bundle through install(FILES), which keeps the
+# RUNPATH they were linked with: CMake's build RUNPATH, the absolute
+# flutter/ephemeral directory of the build tree. Link them with the install
+# RUNPATH instead; libflutter_linux_gtk.so sits next to them in lib/.
+foreach(plugin ${FLUTTER_PLUGIN_LIST})
+  set_target_properties(${plugin}_plugin PROPERTIES
+    BUILD_WITH_INSTALL_RPATH TRUE
+    INSTALL_RPATH "$ORIGIN")
+endforeach(plugin)
+
 
 # === Installation ===
 # By default, "installing" just makes a relocatable bundle in the build
